901:
(a) Any person or entity applying for a bistro dining area permit shall submit a permit application to the city clerk. The application must be made by the owner(s) or lessee(s) of the premises benefiting from the proposed bistro dining area, and shall include the following:
(1) Occupation tax certificate for the eating and drinking establishment;
(2) A certificate of insurance indicating that the applicant currently carries liability insurance in an amount equal to or exceeding $1,000,000.00 and that the City of Sylvania is an additional insured under such policy;
(3) A properly executed indemnity agreement between the applicant and the city in which the applicant agrees to indemnify and save the city harmless from and against any and all liability resulting from or in connection with the applicant's engaging in a bistro dining operation on the city's sidewalk right-of-way;
(4) A site plan sketch showing the location of adjacent private property and adjoining private properties, the area (including square footage) of the city's sidewalk right-of-way for which a permit is sought for bistro dining purposes, and on said sketch, indicate the location of all furniture, including tables and chairs, and, if desired by the applicant, the physical barrier contemplated by subsection 62-103(c), to be used within the proposed bistro dining area such that no furniture or physical barrier will encroach into any tree wells, and must clearly show a minimum of four feet of pedestrian clearance in the remaining portion of the sidewalk not utilized by the bistro dining area;
(5) The address and contact information of the applicant;
(6) An application fee of $0.00.
(b) The annual right-of-way bistro dining area permit fee shall be $0.00 annually.
(c) The bistro dining area permit shall be valid for the remainder of the calendar year in which it is issued, and, if issued after January 1 in any given year, the permit fee shall be prorated for the number of remaining months in the calendar year, including the month that the permit is issued.
(d) Upon approval, the bistro dining area permit shall be specifically limited to the area shown on the site plan included with the application.
(e) A bistro dining area permit may be issued only in conjunction with an eating and drinking establishment.
(f) A bistro dining area permit shall be non-transferrable.
(Ord. No. 503, 3-16-21)

910:
(a) A person or entity applying to place objects within an appearance zone shall submit a permit application to the city clerk. The permit application must be made by the owner(s) or lessee(s) of the premises benefiting from the proposed appearance zone, and shall include the following:
(1) If the applicant is subject to the city's occupation tax, a copy of the application tax certificate for such applicant;
(2) A certificate of insurance demonstrating that the applicant currently carries liability insurance in an amount equaling or exceeding $1,000,000.00, and that the City of Sylvania is an additional insured under such policy;
(3) A properly executed indemnity agreement between the applicant and the city in which the applicant agrees to indemnify and save the city harmless from and against any and all liability resulting from or in connection with the applicant's placing or causing to be placed any objects within the appearance zone;
(4) A site plan sketch showing the location of adjacent private property and adjoining private properties, the area (including square footage) of the city's right-of-way for which the permit is sought, and on said sketch, provide a description of and location of each object to be placed within the appearance zone, and that no such objects will encroach on any tree wells, and must clearly show a minimum of four feet of pedestrian clearance in the remaining portion of the sidewalk not utilized for the appearance zone;
(5) The address and contact information of the applicant; and
(6) An application fee of $0.00.
(b) The annual appearance zone permit shall be $0.00 annually. The permit shall be valid for the remainder of the calendar year in which it is issued, and, if issued after January 1 in any given year, the permit fee shall be prorated for the number of remaining months in the calendar year, including the month that the permit is issued.
(c) Only the following objects may be placed in an appearance zone: planters containing vegetation and seating (benches, chairs, and similar objects), none of which shall be greater than five feet in height. No hanging baskets nor artificial vegetation displays are permitted.
(d) The sidewalk area covered by the permit shall be maintained in a neat and orderly appearance at all times and the area shall be cleared of debris on a daily basis. All objects placed within an appearance zone shall at all times be maintained with a clear and attractive appearance and in good repair.
(e) An appearance zone permit shall be non-transferrable.
(Ord. No. 504, 3-16-21)

